{
  "opening": "The upcoming release introduces significant enhancements to the glom library, focusing on improved data transformation capabilities and better developer experience through clearer representations. Key additions include new spec types for handling defaults, variable capture, and streaming, alongside refinements to existing components like Invoke and the CLI.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The `glom_cli` command-line interface must accept Python-full specifications rather than being limited to AST literals, allowing for more complex logic in specs. The internal functions `mw_get_target` and `mw_handle_target` are exposed to support this extended target handling capability."
    },
    {
      "id": "m29",
      "text": "The public API must expose the `Auto`, `Fill`, `Iter`, and `Let` spec types as specified in the changelog. Additionally, all listed public names such as `Check`, `First`, `GlomError`, `Glommer`, `Inspect`, `Spec`, `TType`, and utility functions like `all`, `chunked`, `dropwhile`, `fill`, `filter`, `first`, `flatten`, `glom`, and `glomit` must be available at their standard import locations."
    },
    {
      "id": "m33",
      "text": "The `Invoke` spec type must provide a concise and readable string representation that omits verbose argument details for clarity."
    },
    {
      "id": "m34",
      "text": "The `Invoke` class must no longer expose its internal `args` attribute as a public member. The module-level constant previously named `consts` must be renamed to `constants` to follow naming conventions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m44",
      "text": "The `Fill` spec type must implement a custom `__repr__` method that returns a human-readable string describing the fill value and mode."
    },
    {
      "id": "m45",
      "text": "The `Assign` spec type must implement a custom `__repr__` method that clearly displays the assignment target and value. The `assign` convenience function must remain accessible under that name."
    },
    {
      "id": "m46",
      "text": "The `Coalesce` spec type must implement a custom `__repr__` method that shows the sources being coalesced. The `Inspect` spec type must also have a reasonable string representation."
    },
    {
      "id": "m47",
      "text": "All public specifier types, including `Auto` and `Check`, must provide reasonable and informative string representations via their `__repr__` methods."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure these behaviors are verified against the public API surface before merging. This release aims to make glom more robust and easier to debug for end users."
}
